1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,085
The reference is the standard hydrogen electrode.

2
00:00:03,085 --> 00:00:16,028
A platinum foil, coated with finely divided platinum black, dips into a one molar solution of hydrogen ions at two ninety eight kelvin, while pure hydrogen gas at one bar bubbles over it.

3
00:00:16,028 --> 00:00:18,268
The platinum does not react.

4
00:00:18,268 --> 00:00:22,278
It only provides a surface for electrons to change hands.

